## Result

**HIGH — unresolved.** R5's compact BASE-blob strategy addresses the demonstrated
metadata self-reference: intake changes the live checkpoint/history, while the
map retains immutable BASE blob digests and reservation captures the later
post-INTENT bytes. The plan also correctly requires a real intake-to-publication
regression, preserves the incoming tip through an ordinary merge, and does not
treat the helper diagnostic as an end-to-end run.

However, R5 changes the live publication authorization semantics while proposing
to retain `CONTROL_VERSION: 10`. This is not merely a compact representation
correction. The current guard unconditionally holds any `publication` operation
for every confirmed issue through `FIX_COMMITTED` (including `FIX_VERIFIED`),
and R5 proposes a new condition under which the named repair publication may
proceed. That is a new executable admission path through a previously mandatory
hold.

